A||||8||Doni Hagan||A "Cadillac MIAMI?"||||1||
Z||000000||Doni Hagan||12-23-2001||06:05 PM||||Yesterday, while driving eastbound on the Indiana Toll Road, I was passed what initially appeared to be a gold notchback GT (it had dual exhaust) with Michigan tags. However, a closer look at the next rest station revealed that the car was badged as a Cadillac MIAMI. It had a 4.5 ltr badge on the back, a Caddy steering wheel, leather seats w/Caddy emblems and a lot more fake wood&chrome in the interior. It even had what appeared to be Seville chrome wheels w/Caddy centers. There wasn't a Pontiac emblem visible anywhere on the car, not even on the sail panels. In all other ways, it was a regular Fiero GT. I waited as long as I could for the driver to come out but was running late. I left my business card stuck in the door and asked the owner to contact me. If he/she does, I'll get pics.<P>I figure some Caddy dealer did a special edition or somehing....I must admit it WAS convincing. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||85 gt fiero||12-23-2001||06:17 PM||||Maybe it was one of the new cadys 4.5 litre v12 with 750 hp <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> anyways it sounds like it looks cool<P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES, LIGHT BARS, SCS SUSPENSION, KONI ADJUSTERS,HIGH POINT CUTOFFS, AND BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
Z||000002||Doni Hagan||12-23-2001||07:43 PM||||This thing was DEFINITELY Fiero based, ribbed trim and all. The "4.5" badge on the back is the same one on late 80's-early 90's Cads. <P>I just got off the phone with someone who said he's seen the same car (or one just like it) in the Dearborn area. He agrees that it's either a "dealer special" or a one-off done by the owner. <P>If I do the N*, I just may consider the idea.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Does anyone know who might own it? A guy who does THAT much work to a Fiero probably knows about PFF.  <p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 12-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTFiero1||12-23-2001||07:57 PM||||that would be sweet if he contacts you. ive been a fan of cadillac and have nvr heard of this. i havea big book of Cadillacs history from 1903-1990 and thre is nothin like that in there. the Allante was its old 2-seater sportscar. i wonder ifit realy came with a 4.5L V-8...<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smoooooth GT||12-23-2001||09:24 PM||||No it did'nt come like that...  It has to be a one -off  that someone did...  How many Pontiac Dealer's that would put forth ANY effort much less THAT much!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||MikeSchaefer||12-24-2001||12:44 AM||||Now why do you suppose someone would even do that?  It's just kind of weird.  I would question whether or not it really has the 4.5, if he lies about what kind of car it is, it wouldn't be too much of a stretch to consider.  Do you think that when people ask what kind of car he drives he actually tells them a Cadillac Miami?  <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cheer_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000006||Doni Hagan||12-24-2001||05:40 PM||||GTFiero1, <P>I, too, am something of a Cadillac afficianado. The bulk of my model collection is dedicated to the marque and I've gathered a small library of Cadillac literature and publications. My goal is to have at least one example from each production year from 1909 to 1979. So far, I've got about 35 years covered (not incl WWII years...no production.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CADDYS.jpg">  <BR>If Cadillac had built such a car, someone somewhere would've mentioned it by now. I'm convinced that the owner did it himself...but still, he did it well. If he's honest about it, he probably says it's a customized Fiero when asked. <P>It's no worse than the Zimmer Quicksilver, which was basically a gussied-up Fiero with a stretch job. Bob's Classics in Florida has one on their website. One of the execs at Skyline Corp. in Elkhart had one a few years ago. Strange little car. WAY too much chrome!<p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Doni Hagan||12-24-2001||08:40 PM||||I just got off the phone with the owner of the mysterious "Cadillac Miami". It in fact started life as an 85 Fiero SE. His son was the one responsible for the modifications. The mother owned an 89 Cadillac Eldorado which was t-boned in 1998. Their son took the engine and installed it in HIS Fiero, along with some of the other stuff I saw on and in the car. It does indeed have a 4.5 ltr engine in it. He had the seats recovered in grey leather and the emblems I saw were from the Eldorado's seats. Also, the wheels are 16" Cadillac optional chrome wheels (I've seen them on the STS.)The father drives the car occasionally as his son has moved overseas (France) and left the car behind. <P>The father used to work for Cadillac Motor Division in HR before retiring in 1999. I've invited him to visit PFF and post a pic of the car. Also, I've been invited to share a beer with him should I visit the Detroit area, which I plan to do in January. If he fails to post a pic by then, I'll take some and post them myself.<P>A mystery solved!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||85 gt fiero||12-24-2001||09:18 PM||||Sweet be sure to get some pics im droolin <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
